From: Keenetic SDK Builder <developers@keenetic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: clamp Jmin to Jmax before drawing a junk packet size

Neither the module nor awg-manager validates Jmin against Jmax on the
kernel path. get_random_u32_inclusive(floor, ceil) computes
floor + get_random_u32_below(ceil - floor + 1): with floor > ceil the
range underflows to ~4G and the drawn size can reach 65535, well past
the jmax-sized buffer; at floor == ceil + 1 the range is 0 and the
compat helper divides by zero.

Applies on top of patch 010, which already guards the kzalloc() result.

Signed-off-by: Keenetic SDK Builder <developers@keenetic.com>
---
--- a/src/send.c
+++ b/src/send.c
@@ -88,7 +88,14 @@
 
 		if (likely(buffer)) {
 			while (junk_packet_count-- > 0) {
-				junk_packet_size = (u16) get_random_u32_inclusive(wg->jmin, wg->jmax);
+				/* Jmin is not validated against Jmax anywhere on the way
+				 * in: with floor > ceil get_random_u32_inclusive()
+				 * underflows its range (and divides by zero at
+				 * floor == ceil + 1), so the size could run past a
+				 * buffer that is only jmax bytes long.
+				 */
+				junk_packet_size = (u16) get_random_u32_inclusive(
+					min(wg->jmin, wg->jmax), wg->jmax);
 
 				get_random_bytes(buffer, junk_packet_size);
 				get_random_bytes(&ds, 1);
